It looks like we share similar concerns regarding Trump's stance on international trade! The notion of prioritizing national interest above all else strikes me as being overly simplistic. We live in an interconnected world; don't you think that kind of approach risks alienating us further?

Additionally, wouldn't that isolationist policy undermine any efforts toward achieving genuine economic progress?

